quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  3,154,"Then He sent upon you peace after distress in the (form of) drowsiness that came over a group of you. In contrast, the other group (i.e. the hypocrites) were worried only about themselves, entertaining evil thoughts about Allah, the thoughts of pagan ignorance. They say: ‘Do we have any role in the matter?’ Say: ‘Indeed, the matter belongs entirely to Allah.’ They hide in their hearts what they do not disclose to you. They say: ‘If we had any say in this matter, we would not have been killed here.’ Say: ‘Even if you were to remain in your homes, those destined to be killed would still have gone to the places where they would die. (It has happened), so that Allah may test what is in your breasts and expose (for the believers) what is in your hearts. And Allah is All-Knowing of what is (hidden) in the breasts."
  3,155,"As for those of you who fled on the day when the two armies met (at the Battle of Uhud), only Satan caused them to slip on account of some of their deeds (i.e. abandoning the positions fixed for the archers). But Allah has now surely forgiven them. Indeed, Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Forbearing."
  3,156,"O believers! Do not be like the disbelievers who say to their brothers when they travel in the land or are engaged in fighting: ‘Had they stayed with us, they would not have died or been slain.’ So Allah will make this (thinking) a cause of regret in their hearts. It is Allah Who gives life and causes death. Allah is All-Seeing of what you do."
  3,157,"If you are slain in the way of Allah or die, surely forgiveness and mercy from Allah would be better than what they accumulate."
